WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.333
A load balancer presents one service interface to a
cluster of workers.

00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:06.652
Imagine a course registration website.

00:00:06.652 --> 00:00:09.338
The browser sends a request to one hostname.

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:15.258
Behind that address, a balancer chooses a worker,
forwards the request, and returns the response.

00:00:15.258 --> 00:00:18.797
The browser does not need to know which worker
handled it.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.506
Round robin rotates through eligible workers.

00:00:21.506 --> 00:00:25.295
With nine requests and three workers, each gets
three requests.

00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:28.362
But equal counts do not mean equal processing time.

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:33.233
One request may return a small cached result;
another may run an expensive query.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:39.006
A least connections policy uses active connections
as a signal, but that signal is still only an

00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:40.329
approximation of work.

00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:43.443
Any worker should be able to serve the next request.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:49.123
If a shopping cart exists only in one worker’s
memory, switching workers may appear to lose it.

00:00:49.123 --> 00:00:54.684
Store durable state outside individual workers, or
explicitly design session affinity and its

00:00:54.684 --> 00:00:55.701
failure behavior.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:01:01.082
A stateless worker is easier to replace, but shared
storage now needs its own capacity and

00:01:01.082 --> 00:01:02.159
availability plan.

00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:06.848
Layer four balancing uses transport information such
as addresses and ports.

00:01:06.848 --> 00:01:12.648
An HTTP layer seven proxy can inspect paths and
headers, terminate TLS, and route to different

00:01:12.648 --> 00:01:13.758
application pools.

00:01:13.758 --> 00:01:15.979
These features cost processing work.

00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:19.250
Actual throughput depends on the system and
workload.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:25.049
Pause here: which layer would you choose to route
slash images and slash checkout to different

00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:25.419
pools?

00:01:25.419 --> 00:01:27.887
An HTTP aware proxy is a natural choice.
